        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'The Bitch',
            subtitle: 'Seven Card Stud Killer Queen',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "The Bitch is a Seven Card Stud poker variant where the Queen of Spades (the 'Bitch') is a game-disrupting card. If the Qâ™  is dealt face-up to any player, the deal immediately stops â€” all cards are thrown in, reshuffled, and redealt to only those players who had not yet folded. At showdown, the entire pot is split between the best high hand and the player holding the Qâ™  face-down in the hole (if anyone has it). If the Qâ™  was never dealt, the best hand wins the whole pot.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "The Bitch is part of the family of Seven Card Stud variants that add special 'kill card' mechanics, alongside games like Chicago, Follow the Queen, and Black Mariah. These variants emerged from American home poker games where players sought to add drama and unpredictability to standard stud.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '2-8 players (standard stud table).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard 52-card deck.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '52-card deck. Poker chips.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard Seven Card Stud deal: 2 cards face-down (hole cards), then cards dealt face-up one at a time with betting rounds between each. 7 cards total per player (2 down, 4 up, 1 down).',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Variations',
            subtitle: 'Known ways this game changes',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'list',
                style: 'unordered',
                items: [
                  {
                    text: 'Wild Bitch: Some play that the Qâ™  in the hole is WILD (can represent any card). In this case, the pot is NOT split â€” best hand wins outright, with Qâ™  as a wild card giving a huge advantage.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Chicago (Related): Seven Card Stud variant where the highest spade in the hole splits the pot with the best hand.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Black Mariah (Related): Seven Card Stud variant with the Qâ™  as a negative card â€” similar kill/penalty mechanics.',
                  },
                ],
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
