        rules: {
          objective: 'Win the pot by having the best 5-card poker hand at showdown, OR by holding the Queen of Spades in the hole.',
          gameplay: 'Ante up. Dealer gives two hole cards face-down and one face-up (third street), then a betting round. Then four more cards are dealt face-up one at a time with a betting round after each (fourth through seventh street). If the Queen of Spades is ever dealt face-up, the hand is killed: cards are thrown in, reshuffled, and redealt to players who had not folded. At showdown, best 5-card hand splits the pot with the player holding Queen of Spades in the hole (if any); if Queen of Spades was never dealt, best hand wins the whole pot.',
          keyRules: [
            'Qâ™  dealt face-up = KILL. Hand stops immediately. Reshuffle and redeal to remaining players.',
            'Qâ™  in the hole (face-down) at showdown = split the pot with the best hand.',
            'If Qâ™  is never dealt at all, best hand wins entire pot.',
            'Players who folded before the kill are eliminated from the redeal.',
            'Standard poker hand rankings apply.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Standard Seven Card Stud fundamentals: play strong starting hands, fold weak ones early. If you have the Qâ™  in the hole, you're guaranteed half the pot at showdown â€” play aggressively.",
          intermediate: "The Qâ™  face-up kill creates an incentive to stay in the hand longer â€” if a redeal occurs, you get a fresh chance with a smaller field. Players who fold early lose this option. However, don't chase the redeal with terrible cards.",
          advanced: "Qâ™  in the hole is essentially a free split pot â€” use it to build the pot aggressively since you're guaranteed at least half. If you have both a strong hand AND Qâ™  in the hole, you can win the entire pot. Watch the board: if all queens have appeared face-up or in mucked hands, no one can hold Qâ™  in the hole.",
          tips: [
            "Holding Qâ™  in the hole is gold â€” you're guaranteed half the pot minimum. Bet and raise aggressively.",
            "If the Qâ™  hasn't appeared by 6th street, it could be in someone's hole cards. Factor this into your pot-splitting evaluation.",
            "Don't fold too early â€” staying in preserves your chance to benefit from a kill/redeal.",
